figdown 0.1 block
# REFUSAL (c), the SECOND shape it takes, and the one worth freezing as a
# golden. `w=`/`h=` were renamed `width=`/`height=` LANGUAGE-WIDE at
# 0.1 — one rule, not one per directive — and on a `node` line BOTH
# spellings are errors: extents live on `pin` (`ELEMENT-GEOMETRY-DIRECTIVE`, and on `size` before it).
# So the rewrite swaps one line error for a DIFFERENT line error on the same
# line, `introducedErrors` sees a message it has not seen before, and the file
# is refused rather than half-migrated.
#
# That is the conservative direction and it is the right one here — moving an
# extent onto a pin line is an author decision, not a rewrite. The fixture
# exists so the behaviour is deliberate rather than accidental: if the refusal
# is ever relaxed to compare error LINES instead of error MESSAGES, this goes
# red, and so does 903, where the swap on one line is the whole defect.
node a "A" w=120 h=60
